{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"Tries","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"Tries"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"],"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"],"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"],"anchor":"Pattern-matching","title":"Pattern matching"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"elements(withPrefix:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"code":"hasPrefix(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"code":"longestPrefix(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For text, the symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type decides what a step is: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps by grapheme cluster, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by scalar, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Character","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s. When the symbols are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were added.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"code":"PrefixTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"PrefixTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a radix tree’s to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with "},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"code":"Trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module beside this one)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"},{"text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" symbols and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" matches: a trie of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns with failure links. Its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property"},{"text":" is the automaton as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"RadixTreeDictionary"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"Trees"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"abstract":[{"text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each state but the root to its failure state. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","isActive":true},{"text":" tells the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apart.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"statesView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV","text":"StatesView","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"statesView"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","nav